-- title:
--   End of the blown-up chart labels one Igusa component prime
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ a prime with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$. Further, $L$ is a field of characteristic zero, $\xi \in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and `hι` requires a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, and `hK` fixes it as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_H$ for the modulus $(q\ell)^2M'$ and the subgroup $H$ which is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$.
--
--   The base $A$ is a Henselian discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field, an $L$-algebra with $L$ as its field of fractions, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`), with $\xi$ in the image of $A$ (`hξA`), and with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. The element $j \in K$ is nonzero and has Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function pushed from $\mathbb{Q}$ to $L$. A uniformiser $\varpi$ of $A$ is fixed by `hϖ`, and `hϖt` provides $\varpi_t \in A$ and a unit $u$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = qu$. Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$, with distinguished element `jChartFin A (↥K) j` the image of $j$.
--
--   The ideal $y$ of $C$ is maximal and contains $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`), and `hss` demands that $j$ be supersingular at $y$: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (a Drinfeld-type local chart datum with equivariance, seven clauses, summarised here) asserts the following for every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A (↥K) j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$) at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` at which the supersingularity condition above holds: there are a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1})v - fu)$ such that: constants from $A$ go to constants $\sigma a$; every level automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ — in the sense of `IsLevelAutAt`, which compares the coefficientwise image of $\tau x$ with the $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M', H)$ translated by `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹` — preserves $C$; such $\tau$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$ act trivially modulo $y'$; each such $\tau$ acting trivially modulo $y'$ is realised by an automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ fixing constants, with linear part a matrix $M$ over $W$ and a scalar $c$ satisfying $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M \equiv c\gamma$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, $c \equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; primes of $S$ over $\sigma\varpi$ with tangent directions $(a_1,b_1)$, $(a_2,b_2)$ not proportional modulo $q$ have distinct contractions to the stalk; for a prime with tangent direction $(1,0)$, a germ from $C$ lies in its contraction exactly when all Laurent coefficients of the corresponding element of $K$ lie in $\mathfrak{m}_A$; and the element [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $C$ and, after subtracting a suitable $a_0 \in A$, is carried to a power series $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e_0 \ge 1$ whose degree-$e_0$ form is a unit at every pair $(a,b)$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   For a fixed such point $z$ (with germ $\varpi_z$ as above, in the maximal ideal of the stalk) and a fixed $y'$ above it satisfying the supersingularity condition, `hy'y` identifies $y'$ with $y$. A concrete witness is then supplied: a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$, $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, series $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1$ congruent to $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the completed stalk with $S := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1})v_1 - f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` is the same list of seven clauses as in `hArig`, for this data.
--
--   The ideal $J$ of $C$ is, by `hJ`, the infimum of the ideals obtained as follows: for $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, take the contraction along $e_1 \circ (\text{completion}) \circ (\text{germ at } z)$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by $\sigma_1\varpi_t$, $X_0$, $X_1$, and pull it back along the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$. The $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$ is, by `hB`, generated over $C$ by the quotients $i/\varpi_t$ with $i \in J$, i.e. the chart of the blow-up of the weighted centre $J$ in the direction $\varpi_t$. The valuation subring $W \subseteq K$ contains $B$ (`hBW`).
--
--   Three hypotheses describe $B$ and $W$: `hR1` states $C \subseteq B$ and that every element of $K$ is a quotient of elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; `hR2` states that $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and that $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) states that $W$ meets $L$ exactly in $A$, that $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b \in C$ one has $b \in y$ if and only if $b \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak{m}_W$ in the sense that $f \in W$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) requires: for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1`) whose kernel is the set of elements of $B$ in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, which is compatible with $A \to k$, and which is equivariant for level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ that preserve $W$, through an element $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ in the kernel `hSubgroup q` of the character $(\gamma,c) \mapsto \det\gamma \cdot c^{q+1}$ and acting by [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325), with $c \ne 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; that level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$ preserve $B$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is hit by translating $\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B$ by some level automorphism attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ after all such translations is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; and that a level automorphism attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $y$ preserves $W$.
--
--   Finally, $O$ is a subring of $K$ which, by `hO`, is an end of the blow-up distinct from $B$: there is a nonzero $a \in J$ such that, with $B_a$ the $A$-subalgebra generated over $C$ by the quotients $i/a$ with $i \in J$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with $O$ the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$, such that every $b \in y$ lying in $O$ is a non-unit there, and such that $B \not\subseteq O$. Moreover $O \subseteq W$ (`hOW`), $O$ is local (`hOloc`) and Noetherian (`hOnoe`), and $C \subseteq O$ (`hCO`). The hypothesis `hIgStab` states that every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ which meets $L$ exactly in $A$, has $\varpi$ in its maximal ideal, contains $C$, and admits an element $c \in C$ with $p(c)$ a unit of $V$ for every monic $p \in A[X]$, is stable under all level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$: $f \in V$ if and only if $\tau f \in V$.
--
--   The conclusion asserts the existence of a prime ideal $\mathfrak{p}$ of $C$ with $\varpi \in \mathfrak{p}$ and $\mathfrak{p} \subseteq y$, $\mathfrak{p} \ne y$, such that for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ satisfying: $V$ meets $L$ exactly in the image of $A$; whenever $\varpi \in V$ it lies in $\mathfrak{m}_V$; and, under the assumption $j \in V$ together with the assumption that for every monic $p \in A[X]$ the value $p(j)$, whenever it lies in $V$, is not in $\mathfrak{m}_V$ — the following two implications hold. First, if $O \subseteq V$, then for every $b \in C$ (whose image lies in $V$) one has $b \in \mathfrak{m}_V$ if and only if $b \in \mathfrak{p}$. Second, if some element of $O$ fails to lie in $V$, then there is a prime ideal $\mathfrak{p}'$ of $C$ with $\varpi \in \mathfrak{p}'$, $\mathfrak{p}' \subseteq y$, $\mathfrak{p}' \ne y$ and $\mathfrak{p}' \ne \mathfrak{p}$, such that for every $b \in C$ (whose image lies in $V$) one has $b \in \mathfrak{m}_V$ if and only if $b \in \mathfrak{p}'$.
--
--   This is the branch-labelling step for the supersingular point $y$ on the integral model of the full-level modular curve: the chosen end $O$ of the blow-up of the weighted centre $J$ lies on exactly one component through $y$, whose prime $\mathfrak{p}$ in the chart algebra it determines, and valuation rings of Igusa type are sorted according to whether they contain $O$, those that do not being centred on a different such prime. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_labelUnit_chartAlgFin_of_end_blowupChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_labelUnit_chartAlgFin_of_end_blowupChart).
